Jian-Feng -

The trick is that you build plots up piece by piece.  I prefer the ggplot commands to qplot so here is a sol'n.

p <- ggplot(data = final.res)
p <- p + geom_linerange(aes(x=position, ymin = 0, ymax = fst, colour = col))
p <- p + geom_point(aes(x = position, y = fst, colour = col))
p <- p + facet_grid(chrom ~., scales = "free_x")
p <- p + scale_x_continuous("chromosome") + scale_y_continuous("SNP density (snps/10k)")
p

-Jonathan

